# C013: Progress getters race with step and finish
#
# CONFIRMED — static analysis (data race / use-after-free)
#
# step() and finish() run with the GIL released (Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS around
# sqlite3_backup_step/finish).  The remaining/page_count getters call
# sqlite3_backup_remaining/pagecount on self->backup WITHOUT acquiring either
# database mutex:
#
#   static PyObject *
#   APSWBackup_get_remaining(...) {
#       return PyLong_FromLong(self->backup ? sqlite3_backup_remaining(self->backup) : 0);
#   }
#
# Concurrent step violates SQLite's getter contract (reading progress while
# step is modifying the backup state).  Concurrent finish can free the handle
# (close_internal sets self->backup = 0) while a getter reads it — a classic
# TOCTOU/use-after-free.
#
# Runtime repro on x86 did not crash in limited testing (strong memory ordering
# makes the race window very small).  TSan would flag this immediately.
